diff --git a/memory/lessons-learned.md b/memory/lessons-learned.md
index d0291e9..6dc4e76 100644
--- a/memory/lessons-learned.md
+++ b/memory/lessons-learned.md
@@ -21,3 +21,4 @@ Format: `- [LESSON-ID] (source_run: <run_id>, evidence: <repo-relative path>, da
 - [L-20261001-DISPATCH-IDS-AS-JSON] (source_run: run-20261001-midimplresume-002, evidence: runs/run-20261001-midimplresume-002/logs/policy-events.jsonl, date: 2026-10-01, tags: dispatch,dispatch-prompt,hooks) Write a staged subagent's dispatch inputs as a JSON object ("task_id": "...", "run_id": "...") in the Agent prompt, not as markdown bullets: the pre_dispatch_check hook extracts only JSON-quoted task_id/run_id pairs and refuses a dispatch whose identifiers it cannot find, before any precondition artifact is checked.
 - [L-20261001-WRITE-TOOL-FOR-EVIDENCE-FILES] (source_run: run-20261001-midimplresume-002, evidence: runs/run-20261001-midimplresume-002/logs/policy-events.jsonl, date: 2026-10-01, tags: hooks,evidence-retention,orchestration) Use the Write tool, not Bash echo/heredoc redirects, for orchestrator request and attempt-source files whose content mentions the target repo directory: the skill_enforcement hook treats any Bash command whose text names that directory alongside a write as an attempted application-source edit and refuses it, even when the target file is under runs/.
 - [L-20261001-MEMORY-APPLIED-NEEDS-CITING-EVIDENCE] (source_run: run-20261001-midimplresume-002, evidence: runs/run-20261001-midimplresume-002/logs/policy-events.jsonl, date: 2026-10-01, tags: memory,evidence-retention,validation) record_memory_applied requires its evidence_path file to literally contain the applied entry_id; a dispatch prompt that merely acts on a lesson without naming it is refused. Retain a decision policy event that names the entry id (e.g. resume_command_id_sequencing with memory_entry) first, then cite logs/policy-events.jsonl as the evidence_path.
+- [L-20261003-RESUME-DISCLOSE-ORPHAN-EDITS] (source_run: run-20261002-obsidianlive-004, evidence: runs/run-20261002-obsidianlive-004/logs/policy-events.jsonl, date: 2026-10-03, tags: resume,engineer,tdd,dispatch-prompt) Before dispatching a fresh Engineer for a restarted Implementation phase, run git status and git diff on the target repo yourself. An interrupted Engineer may have left uncommitted in-scope edits that the checkpoint does not record. Name those edits in the fresh Engineer's dispatch prompt so it reads them and decides independently whether to adopt or revise them, rather than discovering unexplained changes mid-protocol. Then apply the normal TDD orchestration check (test-only change, no source change) before mediating its pre-test. Never revert the orphaned edits through orchestrator Bash.
